WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.134
-Here's how it works.

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:04.270
we each have two envelopes
containing confessions.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.639
One is true.
The other is a lie.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.873
Once you read your confession,

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:09.942
the other two players
get to interrogate you,

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:12.112
and then they have to come up
with a unanimous decision.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:14.280
Is it the truth, or is it a lie?

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.615
-Ooh.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:18.250
-Matthew, you'll go first.
-Ooh.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.086
What envelope should he open,
number one or number two?

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.421
-Oh, which one.
-I think we should say...

00:00:22.421 --> 00:00:23.656
-Number two.
-...number two.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.024
-Yeah, yeah.
-Number two.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.025
-Two.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.127
-See what we've got here.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.463
I once ate...
[ Laughs ]

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.199
[ Laughter ]
I once ate peyote

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.202
in a cage with a mountain lion.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.871
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:41.207
-Okay.
Can I start with a question?

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.208
-Yes, of course.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.543
-What in God's name is peyote?

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:46.112
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, I know.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.247
Peyote is, like,
some type of hallucinogenic.

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:50.416
-It's a spiritual --
-Oh, it's a drug.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.685
-You were in a c--
What year was this?

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.520
-What year was this?
-Yeah, when was it?

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.522
-14 years ago.

00:00:56.522 --> 00:01:00.426
-Yeah, and how could you be
in a cage with a mountain lion?

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:02.161
-Well, that was the easy part.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.496
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.498
-Did the mountain lion
take any peyote.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.001
-[ Laughs ]
-I will say this --

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.902
four hours later,
the mountain lion was

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:14.307
cuddled up with me and purring.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.376
-He's such a good actor.
I'm freaking out. Uh, wait.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.478
What would make you do this?
And was it a mistake?

00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:24.016
-No, it was one of
the more thrilling escapades

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.286
of my life, actually.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.788
-Did you pay someone to do this?

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.891
-No, no, this was just me
and the mountain lion.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:35.061
-Do you take a lot of drugs?
-It was not filmed. [ Laughs ]

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.396
-No, I do not.

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:39.098
-What do you think?

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:41.601
-Well, I think he is
quite druggy so...

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.603
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.372
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:49.108
-Right, but peyote with
a mountain lion is dangerous,

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:51.944
so he could be
a little dangerous, too.

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:56.416
-He may have thought
he saw a lion.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:02:00.586
-I'm going to go with true.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:01.754
-Okay.
I'll say true, as well.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.088
-That is true.

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:04.090
[ Cheers and applause ]
-[ Laughing ] Wait, what?

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.258
-What?!

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:07.594
-Are you kidding me?

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.595
-It was in Mexico, if that helps

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.764
to believe the story.
-Oh, in Mexico.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.532
-Ah, of course.
Anything happens...

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:15.100
Are you serious?
-Yes.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.469
Were you freaking out?

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.304
-No, that's why it worked out.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.772
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:20.773
If I would have freaked out,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.276
it probably wouldn't
have worked out.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.211
-Was the lion menacing
at any stage?

00:02:26.211 --> 00:02:28.848
-At the beginning.
-Wow.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.517
-But we got on
the same frequency.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.385
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:35.221
-Alright, alright, alright.
-Oh, my God!

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.090
-We got on the mammalian
frequency

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.190
and things all --
like I said,

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.859
he ended up purring...

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:40.959
-Oh, my...
-...just scratching him

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:42.962
behind the ears
four hours later.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.196
Everyone should try it
at least once.

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:45.999
-Alright. Which one should
I open, One or two.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.167
-Two, two!
-One! One! One!

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.669
-One?
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.371
-One.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.777
-I got hit by a car
at full speed and survived.

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:01.113
[ Chuckles ]
-No, you didn't.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:03.049
No, you didn't.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:05.884
What's full speed?

00:03:05.884 --> 00:03:08.287
Like a Matchbox car?
-I'd say probably...

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:10.556
-Hot wheels?

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.558
Regular size automobile?
-Yeah, sure.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:13.692
Regular size.

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:15.461
I'd say it was like
an SUV, maybe.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:16.895
-SUV, maybe.

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:19.332
-It was going very fast.
-What year was this?

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:23.502
-I'd say it was probably
10 years ago maybe --

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:25.338
-Were you doing peyote?

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.706
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.707
-No, I was not doing peyote.

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:32.378
-Did you go under the car
or over the top?

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.613
-[ Chuckles ]
-A minor detail --

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.481
-Are you picturing me
flipping over it?

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.483
No, you know what happened,
is I -- No, I didn't --

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.818
I didn't --
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.152
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:42.154
-I kind of grazed it.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.190
I grazed the mirror.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.525
-So, it didn't really hit you
at full speed.

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:49.362
-I spun around,
and my shoes came off.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.197
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.532
-You were in flip-flops, though.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.700
-No, I was into, like,
clogs at this time.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.635
-Ah, they were untied
anyway, though.

00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:58.604
-They were tied up.
-Mm!

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.940
-What else were you wearing
besides clogs?

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.675
-[ Chuckles ]
I was wearing jeans.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.344
-Did you have underwear on
under those jeans.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:07.179
-Yeah, for a moment.

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:10.016
No, I did, yeah.
-Were those underwear the --

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.317
Were they still clean
after the collision?

00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:13.619
-Yeah, no.
-Questions --

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.588
-The story is false.
It's false.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.689
-It is false.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:17.990
-For a start,
you weren't really hit.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.859
If anything, you were brushed.
-It just nicked you.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:22.561
[ Laughter ]
-The story is true.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:26.331
I did get hit by an SUV
going like 60 in Manhattan.

00:04:26.331 --> 00:04:29.668
We were leaving a bar with
my friend, who works here.

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.537
He can actually vouch for me.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.539
And I'm leaving, and I was
like, "I'll get a cab,"

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.241
and I walked into the street,
and this car went --

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:36.709
And it was just speeding down,

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.211
and I ripped the mirror
off the car

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:40.546
because it was going that fast.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.415
-How is your arm?
-I had a giant gash.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.917
-Could it have been deliberate?
Was it Colbert?

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.752
[ Laughter ]
-It was not --

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:51.257
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.793
-Stephen Colbert...

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.894
This is before we had shows on
at the same time.

00:04:55.894 --> 00:04:57.630
He would never do that
to me back then.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.732
Alright, here we go.
Hugh, it is your turn.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.133
Oh, yeah.
One or two?

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.902
-2.

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:05.404
-2.
-2 again.

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:07.106
Alright.

00:05:09.908 --> 00:05:12.144
As a child,
I had a compulsion

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:15.047
to stick apple peel up my nose,

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:17.450
and I spent many happy hours
having it removed

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.786
by London's finest doctors.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:21.353
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:22.989
-This already sounds very true.

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.490
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.091
-How old were you?
How old were you?

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:27.560
-I was 34.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.429
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:32.965
I guess I was 5 or so.
-But why would you --

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.400
'Cause you had no toys?
Were you bored?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.468
You wanted
to see what would happen?

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:36.602
-I think I know what it was.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:37.970
I had an uncle
who used to do that thing,

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.972
where he wanted
to pick his nose,

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.340
but he was too polite,

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.843
so he used to do it with
a sort of hanky, you know,

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.745
and I think I was impressed.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:49.181
why I transferred from hanky
to apple peel,

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:51.184
I don't know, but I did,

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:52.652
and I quite enjoyed
the experience,

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:54.786
and I repeated it.
-So, wait. You kept shoving --

00:05:54.786 --> 00:05:57.223
Did Mom or Dad know
you had them up your nose?

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:59.225
-Yeah, I'd say,
"I've done it again,"

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.793
and back we went

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:03.262
to the ear, nose,
and throat specialist.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.264
-Damn it, Hugh,
you've done it again.

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:06.498
You've done it again.
-Yeah.

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:08.100
-I think it happened.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.935
-[ Laughing ] You do?
-I think it's true, right?

00:06:09.935 --> 00:06:11.237
I think he's --

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.239
I think he's pulling
our Johnson.

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.541
-He's saying false.
He said it didn't happen.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.776
I agree with Matthew.
It did not happen.

00:06:17.776 --> 00:06:18.944
-Well, of course it happened.

00:06:18.944 --> 00:06:20.312
Of course it did.

00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:21.480
-It did happen.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.484
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.786
Bad kid.
You're a bad child.

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:28.887
You're a bad child.

00:06:28.887 --> 00:06:30.323
Our thanks
to Matthew McConaughey,

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:31.224
Hugh Grant.

